  "name": "exit code 4 is overloaded: not-a-slopwork-repo vs ref-not-found are indistinguishable",
  "slug": "exit-code-4-is-overloaded",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "exit code 4 is overloaded: not-a-slopwork-repo vs ref-not-found are indistinguishable",
    "details_md": "requireRepoRoot throws NOT_FOUND(4) for a missing .slop/ (src/repo/paths.ts:82) while docs define 4 strictly as ref-did-not-resolve. Also slop web breaks the convention the other way: its own findSlopRoot walk throws GENERIC_ERROR(1) (src/cli/commands/web.ts:74). Pick one semantic, use requireRepoRoot in web, document it.",
    "acceptance": [
      "web uses the shared repo-root discovery + same exit code",
      "docs/README exit-code table matches behavior for the not-a-repo case"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/repo/paths.ts:82",
      "src/cli/commands/web.ts:32"
    ],
